.SH NAME
.PP
reelect \- reelect the master in the server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]stp.reelect([options])\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
Stp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to reelect the master node in the server group where the
current STP node is located.
The number of surviving nodes in the server group must exceed 1/2 of the total
number of nodes in other to be elected.
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
options ( \f[I]object, optional\f[] )
.PP
Other optional parameters can be set through the option parameter:
.IP \[bu] 2
Seconds (number): Specify the election timeout period, the election will be
completed within the specified time, the unit is seconds, the default value is
30.
.RS 2
.PP
The value of this parameter must be greater than or equal to 10.
Otherwise an error will be reported when the relevant statement is executed.
.PP
Format: \f[C]Seconds: 60\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
HostName (string): Specify the host name of the desired master node.
.RS 2
.PP
Format: \f[C]HostName: "sdbserver"\f[]
.RE
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, there is no return value.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
